# Keep host build output out of the Docker build context. Without this, `COPY src/ src/` in
# deploy/Dockerfile copies the Windows-generated bin/ and obj/ folders into the image, clobbering
# the container's own `dotnet restore` output. The `--no-restore` publish then reads a
# project.assets.json full of Windows paths (C:\Program Files (x86)\...\Shared\NuGetPackages) and
# fails with "Unable to find fallback package folder". The container restores cleanly on its own,
# so these never belong in the context.
**/bin/
**/obj/

# Version control and IDE cruft — no reason to ship it into the build.
.git/
.gitignore
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.user

# The image builds its own EF migration bundles and publishes fresh; local publish/artifacts,
# test results, and logs would only bloat the context.
**/publish/
**/TestResults/
**/*.log
